{"format":1,"key":"zone:westfall","path":"/lore/zone/westfall","name":"Westfall","kind":"zone","label":"Zone","zone":{"key":"westfall","name":"Westfall","path":"/lore/zone/westfall"},"levels":"Levels 10-20","description":"Once the fertile breadbasket of the Kingdom of Stormwind, Westfall has collapsed into a windswept, neglected territory overrun by outlaws. Deprived of…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:westfall","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["Once the fertile breadbasket of the Kingdom of Stormwind, Westfall has collapsed into a windswept, neglected territory overrun by outlaws. Deprived of official crown support and military garrisons, its surviving homesteaders cling to their farms while the Defias Brotherhood tightens its grip from the abandoned mining town of Moonbrook.","For generations, Westfall fed the Kingdom of Stormwind. Its rolling pastures and wheat fields flourished until the aftermath of the Second War brought financial exhaustion and political neglect. When the kingdom poured its resources elsewhere and failed to maintain its garrisons, the territory grew fallow. Today, barren pastures, howling coastal gusts, rogue harvest golems, and raiding Riverpaw gnolls make daily survival a constant trial for the stubborn few who refuse to abandon their homesteads.","Westfall's collapse accelerated when the Stonemasons Guild, denied payment for rebuilding Stormwind City, turned to open revolt. Outlawed and exiled under Edwin VanCleef, the stonemasons reconstituted themselves as the Defias Brotherhood. They claimed Westfall as their stronghold, burning stubborn farmers' fields, salting soil, and seizing abandoned mines. Operating out of the ghost town of Moonbrook, the Brotherhood now rules the majority of the countryside in all but name.","With the House of Nobles ignoring Westfall's plight, local inhabitants took up their own defense. Based at the fortified post of Sentinel Hill, Gryan Stoutmantle organized the People's Militia—a volunteer force attempting to hold the line against gnolls and bandits. Lacking formal soldiers and supplies from Stormwind, the Militia relies on wandering adventurers to push back the Defias tide and protect the remaining farms."],"hash":"51e782","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"b63fb14d1f","sec":102},"female-narrator":{"sha":"4dc4cb5851","sec":105}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Westfall (Classic)","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Westfall_(Classic)"},{"kind":"wiki","title":"Westfall","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Westfall"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/npc/gryan-stoutmantle","n":"Gryan Stoutmantle","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/npc/edwin-vancleef","n":"Edwin VanCleef","k":"boss"},{"p":"/lore/topic/defias-brotherhood","n":"Defias Brotherhood","k":"topic"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/sentinel-hill","n":"Sentinel Hill","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/moonbrook","n":"Moonbrook","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/deadmines","n":"The Deadmines","k":"dungeon"},{"p":"/lore/quest/12-the-peoples-militia","n":"The People's Militia","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/quest/36-westfall-stew","n":"Westfall Stew","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/zone/elwynn","n":"Elwynn Forest","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/forest-s-edge","n":"Forest's Edge","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/jerod-s-landing","n":"Jerod's Landing","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/thunder-falls","n":"Thunder Falls","k":"subzone"}],"children":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/alexston-farmstead","n":"Alexston Farmstead","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/dagger-hills","n":"Dagger Hills","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/dead-acre","n":"Dead Acre","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/deadmines","n":"Deadmines","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/defias-hideout","n":"Defias Hideout","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/demont-s-place","n":"Demont's Place","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/dust-plains","n":"Dust Plains","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/furlbrow-s-pumpkin-farm","n":"Furlbrow's Pumpkin Farm","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzo